# Dan Sensecall

> Dan Sensecall is a UK-based freelance UX designer and service design consultant. He works with government, public sector and charity teams on user-centred services.

## About and experience

- [About Dan Sensecall](https://sensecall.co.uk/about/): Background and information about Dan.
- [CV](https://sensecall.co.uk/cv/): Professional experience, skills and education.

## Work and expertise

- [Projects](https://sensecall.co.uk/projects/): Selected UX and service design case studies.
- [Service design](https://sensecall.co.uk/service-design/): Dan's approach to practical service design.
- [Ways to work with me](https://sensecall.co.uk/services/): Contract design on a delivery team, regular fractional support, specialist input for bids and partners, or an independent product and service review.
- [Public sector service design consultant](https://sensecall.co.uk/public-sector-service-design-consultant/): Specialist service design, UCD and UX expertise for public-sector bids, frameworks, technical-assistance assignments and delivery consortia.
- [Fractional product and service design](https://sensecall.co.uk/fractional-product-service-design/): Senior product and service design support for a few days a month or week: making sense of complex services, agreeing priorities and supporting designers.
- [Independent product and service reviews](https://sensecall.co.uk/product-service-review/): A focused outside view of a product, service or proposed direction, with prioritised recommendations.
- [Writing](https://sensecall.co.uk/writing/): Articles about design, research, product ownership and digital delivery.

